  "description": "Publish generated story evidence that preserves family boundaries, negative results and each material candidate's completed evidence path without changing production code itself.\n\n## Background\n\nThe report presents shifts, QC construction, generic puncturing and interleaving as separate workload families. It derives numeric statements from committed machine-readable artifacts, identifies actual production consumers, records QC runtime rotation as inapplicable, keeps the ETSI [Etsi2015] bit-interleave permutation distinct from the other interleavers, preserves the accepted AFF3CT [Cassagne2019] NR no-win while `prepare_llrs` is unchanged, and treats withdrawn DVB warm receipts against xdsopl `PCTITL` [Xdsopl2026] only as history. A family whose profile nominates no form ends at that profile. A family whose profile nominates a material form reaches this report only through the candidate implementation and confirmation leaves its nomination requires, and this report sits behind their terminal sinks in the dependency graph. The residual `BitVec` shift family is the one with such a path: its BMI2-gated funnel candidate carries the A/B confirmation whose outcome this report publishes, and the AVX2 lane-crossing funnel the same profile nominated is feasible at the MSRV, unselected for implementation in this epic, and preserved here as an outcome rather than dropped.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: A deterministic generator reproduces the publication tables from committed receipts, profiles and content-pinned dispositions, including latency, throughput, whole-consumer costs, intervals, sample counts, conversion stages and runtime provenance where applicable.\n- [hard] REQ-02: The findings map every story criterion to durable evidence and preserve the QC inapplicability, generic-puncturing separation, NR accepted no-win, unavailable mappings, withdrawn DVB evidence and profile no-win outcomes.\n- [hard] REQ-03: Each family's disposition reaches this report through its own graph path: a profile nominating no form ends at that profile, while a material nomination's candidate implementation and confirmation work is complete and this report sits behind its terminal sink in the instantiated dependency graph.\n- [hard] REQ-04: This report and the story stay open while a material nomination lacks its planning-time Rust 1.95 compile, assembly and scalar-fallback feasibility record, its reviewed amended manifest, its exact instantiated dependencies or its completed candidate evidence.\n- [hard] REQ-05: Each performance claim cites its accepted receipt and protocol identity, while each absent comparison has an explicit semantic or consumer reason.\n- [hard] REQ-06: The report states the residual-shift candidate's outcome as its confirmation's acceptance summary records it, qualifying or not, together with the retention decision the frozen rule produces, and records the nominated AVX2 lane-crossing funnel as feasible at the MSRV, not selected for implementation in this epic, and the reason for that selection.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe report stays in the story's development area; permanent prose cites it rather than copying volatile measurements.\n\nSource references: [Cassagne2019], [Etsi2015], [Xdsopl2026].",
